                <pb facs="0132" n="38" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg38"/>

                <head>No. 36.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Tree</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-04-13"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 13,
                        1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 81.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch No. 224, of the 28th ultimo,
                    reporting your course in refusing to grant to Mr. Charles G. Richter a passport
                    upon the ground that he has been absent from this country for sixteen years and
                    has no fixed intentions of returning at anytime in the future, has been
                    received. Your action in the premises is approved by the Department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
